--- Arm P, hypothesis (ii) MOMENTUM-CONSERVING (medium alone)
    P1 contact:  opacity needed for the contact to switch on where <a> = a0
      canonical kappa = 4.6781e-09 kpc^2/Msun = 22.40 cm^2/g = 3.747e-23 cm^2/proton
                 mfp(z=1100) = 2.554e-02 kpc = 25.5 pc ;  Gamma/H = 0.84 (z1100), 4.58 (z3400)
                 Bullet: ICM column 0.006-0.03 g/cm^2 -> 0.13 - 0.67 optical depths
      alt       kappa = 3.8709e-09 kpc^2/Msun = 18.54 cm^2/g = 3.100e-23 cm^2/proton
                 mfp(z=1100) = 3.087e-02 kpc = 30.9 pc ;  Gamma/H = 0.70 (z1100), 3.79 (z3400)
                 Bullet: ICM column 0.006-0.03 g/cm^2 -> 0.11 - 0.56 optical depths
      => Arm P1 FIRES: it breaks (ii) by a direct coupling and then fails (1) (drag ~ H at
         z = 1100, when the cold component must stay decoupled) and (2) (dragged with the
         gas, where RB1 puts the mass with the galaxies).

      P2 no material identity: the carrier of Pi is the SOURCED FIELD, not a substance.
         It interpenetrates because fields SUPERPOSE: two halos' fields add, and the lensing
         charge follows each cluster's own baryons. => (2) PASSES, (4) PASSES.
         Price: (1) FAILS -- the carrier has no conserved cold rest mass:
           canonical log M_b 10.45 : M_c/M_b = 41.49 at 272 kpc, 97.83 at 637 kpc ; budget 5.41 -> excess 7.7x / 18.1x
           canonical log M_b 10.90 : M_c/M_b = 24.51 at 272 kpc, 58.07 at 637 kpc ; budget 5.41 -> excess 4.5x / 10.7x
           alt       log M_b 10.45 : M_c/M_b = 45.66 at 272 kpc, 107.60 at 637 kpc ; budget 5.41 -> excess 8.4x / 19.9x
           alt       log M_b 10.90 : M_c/M_b = 27.00 at 272 kpc, 63.89 at 637 kpc ; budget 5.41 -> excess 5.0x / 11.8x
         M_c(<r) grows ~ r without bound: the settled halo is PHANTOM, not substance.

--- Arm S, hypothesis (iii) NORMALLY SELF-GRAVITATING
     A component whose density does not gravitate cannot be 'at full share' in clusters
     (RB1 gate 1, f_ret -> 1) and cannot supply the lensing mass at all: deficit = the
     whole cold share, a factor 5.4 below the law's demand at 272 kpc and 5.4 at 637 kpc.
     And it is still a material continuum, so it cannot interpenetrate: (2) fails too.
     => Arm S FIRES.

--- Arm M5', the multi-stream escape
     N mutually transparent, cosmologically MIXED identical elastic constituents: every
     constituent carries 1/N of the mass and 1/N of the stress, hence the SAME map R(r).
     In the overlap of two passing halos the preimage of the overlap is, for EACH
     constituent, TWO disjoint Lagrangian regions: its map is 2-to-1. A material continuum
     has an injective map, and by continuity det F must vanish on the way: it folds.
     c_L^2 crosses zero at y = 6/5 and diverges at y = 9/7 (3lam+2mu = J/(7y/3-3)), so
     the fold is not a benign crossing -- the longitudinal mode is imaginary across it.
     Segregation by halo (A all in constituent 1, B all in 2) needs one constituent per
     halo that ever merges: ~10^11 species = labelled dust, and dust has sigma_r^2 >= 0.
     => The escape closes on itself.  Arm M5' FIRES.

####################################################################################################
# Q4  what sigma_r^2 < 0 then means
####################################################################################################
    canonical log M_b 10.45 : v_inf =  136.8 km/s ; the law requires sigma_r^2 = -9.3525e+03 (km/s)^2 = -(96.7 km/s)^2 = -(v_inf/sqrt2)^2
    canonical log M_b 10.90 : v_inf =  177.2 km/s ; the law requires sigma_r^2 = -1.5701e+04 (km/s)^2 = -(125.3 km/s)^2 = -(v_inf/sqrt2)^2
    alt       log M_b 10.45 : v_inf =  143.4 km/s ; the law requires sigma_r^2 = -1.0281e+04 (km/s)^2 = -(101.4 km/s)^2 = -(v_inf/sqrt2)^2
    alt       log M_b 10.90 : v_inf =  185.8 km/s ; the law requires sigma_r^2 = -1.7260e+04 (km/s)^2 = -(131.4 km/s)^2 = -(v_inf/sqrt2)^2

   (a) Kinetic reading: P_r = int f v_r^2 d^3v is >= 0 for every f >= 0. The law demands
       P_r = -J < 0, i.e. a NEGATIVE MEASURE: f < 0 on a set carrying second moment
       |sigma_r^2| = (v_inf/sqrt2)^2, which is -1/2 of the halo's own v_inf^2. No kinetic
       medium -- cold, warm, hot, collisional, collisionless or anisotropic -- can do this.
   (b) Maxwell reading: in the deep field
         sigma = -Pi -> diag(+J, -J, -J) = T[phi],  grad phi = g,
       i.e. tension ALONG the field equal to the energy density (w_par = -1) and equal
       transverse pressure: the canonical (Maxwell) stress of a classical field.
   (c) Therefore: the carrier of the law's static halo is the FIELD. The 'cold dark energy'
       of form B is that field's polarization charge (phantom mass), and rho_c is NOT a
       conserved rest-mass density -- M_c(<r) ~ r diverges, which is exactly the amount gap
       AMT1 measured at the KiDS radii.

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
   K1 (strain |u| >> 1, not elastic)   : FIRES
   K2 (Bullet: homeomorphism / yield)  : FIRES
   K3 (property 1: no conserved mass)  : FIRES  <-- the price of the only surviving carrier
   K4 (property 3: a field is not hot) : FIRES
   K5 (locality is forced)              : FIRES
   K7 (multi-stream escape)             : FIRES
   K6 (sound speeds)                    : HOLDS  <-- real, subluminal, no ghost

   WHICH HYPOTHESIS MUST BREAK:  (ii) MOMENTUM-CONSERVING (the medium alone).
     (i)   LOCAL -- forced. Smoothing the field destroys the equilibrium (Arm N), and
           locality never touches (2), so dropping it buys nothing there.
     (iii) NORMALLY SELF-GRAVITATING -- required by (1) and (3). A component whose
           density does not gravitate is not at full share in clusters (Arm S).
     (ii)  is the ONLY break compatible with (2): interpenetration forbids a material
           continuum, and the one carrier of Pi left is a field -- which is not a closed
           system (it is sourced by, and reacts back on, the baryons).
   IS IT CONSISTENT WITH THE FOUR PROPERTIES?  Partly, and that is the finding:
     (2) PASSES, (4) PASSES, (3) FAILS, (1) FAILS -- the carrier is not a substance,
     so there is no conserved cold 5.41 x baryon component to be carried.

   => the class of media is CLOSED. sigma_r^2 < 0 is a RADIAL TENSION along grad Phi
      (= the field's Maxwell tension), not a velocity dispersion.

